From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:22:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Type Authorization-Lifetime as Unsigned32

RFC 6733 section 8.9: 'The Authorization-Lifetime AVP (AVP Code 291) is
of type Unsigned32'; the AVP table in section 4.5 agrees. As Integer32,
lifetimes from 2^31 seconds up decode as negative numbers.
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..fa3c7ea 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -1754,7 +1754,7 @@
 		</avp>
 		<!-- 288-290    Unallocated http://www.iana.org/assignments/aaa-parameters  -->
 		<avp name="Authorization-Lifetime" code="291" mandatory="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-bit="mustnot">
-			<type type-name="Integer32"/>
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
 		</avp>
 		<avp name="Redirect-Host" code="292" mandatory="must" may-encrypt="no" protected="may" vendor-bit="mustnot">
 			<type type-name="DiameterURI"/>
